From 0816630a54c232ec5ab328aa1965794ce4ec08a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 10:30:01 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08291/11362] [outer-loop] exp6110: sc25/g50t frontier collapse
 is hidden-state aliasing; k-suffix state key de-aliases (default OFF)

DIAGNOSIS (offline, frames-only, sc25): all 8 root candidates are visually inert on their
FIRST application -- the game consumes the action while hidden state advances (first visible
frame change at repeat-depth 2 for 5/8 actions; ANY inert prefix changes a later action's
outcome, 6/6 pairs). The generic node_id hashes the whole grid, so every successor aliases
into the root node, the untested list drains, and the search ends at 24 expansions / 1
"distinct" state -- identically at 6000 and 30000 (exp6094). Of the three candidate
mechanisms (masked-region hashing / whole-frame-but-hidden-state / dropped facing-registers)
the measurement selects the second: no mask was active, and the working sc25 adapter key
adds game-internal registers the frames do not expose.

FIX: graph_explore_solve_v2 node key = frame hash + last-k own actions of the arriving path
(the classic k-th-order remedy for a non-Markov observation). Generic by construction --
frames + the agent's own actions only, no game ids, no per-game constants. DEFAULT OFF:
CARNOT_ARC_STATE_KEY_SUFFIX_K env flag (explicit state_key_action_suffix_k param overrides);
k=0 is byte-identical to the shipped single-hash identity. Both-directions test:
tests/python/test_arc_state_key_suffix_gate_2026_08_05.py (6 passed).

MEASURED (adapter-free, census budget 6000, deterministic; artifact
results/outer_loop_arc_state_key_suffix_ab_20260805.json):

  game  k  expansions  states  distinct_frames  explored_out  level  actions
  sc25  0     24          1          1            COLLAPSE      0      -
  sc25  1   6000       2024        358            budget wall   0      -
  g50t  0   4100        843        843            COLLAPSE      0      -
  g50t  1   6000       1230        401            budget wall   0      -
  ls20  0   1777        538        538            solved        1     13
  ls20  1   4793       1464        538            solved        1     13
  tu93  0   2114        591        591            solved        1     18
  tu93  1   4346       1220        591            solved        1     18

VERDICT: helps on the collapse class, with a measured cost that justifies default-OFF.
sc25 is the clean win (1 -> 358 real frames; representation limit removed; L1 still needs
more than 6000 expansions). g50t stops collapsing but real-frame coverage at fixed budget
falls 843 -> 401 (suffix duplicates consume budget). Controls do not regress on outcome
(same levels, same shortest paths) but pay 2.7x / 2.1x expansions. k=1 is a per-game lever
for frontier-collapsed games, not a new universal default.

CPU only, offline arcade only, no game played on any scored endpoint, no hidden-game source
read. The live scored path (E3AgentPolicy StepwiseExplorer._hash) shares this aliasing class
and is the natural follow-up, gated the same way.

